==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|baby-sitter}}
* {{alter|en|baby sitter||rare}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|baby|sitter}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈbeɪbiˌsɪtɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-babysitter.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s}}

# A person who [[care]]s for one or more [[baby|babies]] or [[child]]ren for a short period of time in place of their [[guardian|legal guardian]]s.
#: {{syn|en|sitter}}
#: {{hyper|en|childminder}}
#: {{ux|en|My neighbor is sometimes a '''babysitter''' for other mothers’ children.}}
# {{lb|en|derogatory}} A person who has to [[watch]] or [[attend]] to anything or anyone unnecessarily closely; a [[coddler]] or [[handholder]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Alan Ball|title=Playing Extra Time|page=158
|passage=He said he did not want to be on tenterhooks worrying about us and having to act as a '''babysitter''' for grown men.}}

